<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Tauri signs with the hardened runtime by default, and under it the microphone is an
         entitlement before it is a permission. Without this key tccd refuses the request in
         about 12ms with no dialog — logged as "requires entitlement
         com.apple.security.device.audio-input but it is missing" — so recording fails and
         nothing on screen says why.

         Screen recording, Accessibility and Input Monitoring need no entitlement; they are
         permissions only.

         The hardened runtime also turns on library validation, and without an Apple team that
         refuses every dylib that is not Apple's — including one signed with this app's own
         certificate. Nothing like that is bundled today. Adding one (Sparkle, a sidecar
         framework) needs com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation here as well. -->

    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
